lly measured at the present value of lease payments over the lease term plus initial direct costs, if any. If a lease does not provide a discount rate and the rate cannot be readily determined, an incremental borrowing rate is used to determine the present value of future lease payments. Lease and variable non-lease components within the Company&#8217;s lease agreements are accounted for separately. The Company has no material leases in which the Company is the lessor.</span></p><p style="text-indent:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:12pt;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The Company&#8217;s leasing arrangements are classified as operating leases, for which expense is recognized on a straight-line basis. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">, total </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;"><span style="-sec-ix-hidden:F_15b28162-fc61-4628-9288-cb4011487274;"><span style="-sec-ix-hidden:F_020e8e5e-241c-4875-9615-a8e53666df33;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">ROU</span></span></span></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> assets were </span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">$</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_bca14d8d-613d-493a-ac9d-49fb1a59e64a" contextRef="C_a1ace55e-f041-4237-a88a-4db5d471a18f" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseRightOfUs